WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.920
Lay Matthew, Mark and Luke side by
side, and something odd appears.

2
00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:09.710
In one healing story, all three break
off Jesus' sentence at exactly the same

3
00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:12.020
point, with the same aside.

4
00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:14.880
Elsewhere, Matthew and
Luke share whole sayings,

5
00:00:14.930 --> 00:00:17.970
word for word, that Mark
doesn't have at all.

6
00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:19.760
So who copied whom?

7
00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:23.190
And is there a lost source
that nobody has ever found?

8
00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:27.650
In this mission, you'll sort the
Gospels' material into what all 3 share,

9
00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:30.580
what 2 share, and what only 1 has.

10
00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:35.000
Then you'll test rival theories,
drawn as arrows between the Gospels.

11
00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:39.970
Your mission: work out who copied whom,
and whether a lost source is needed.
